  "id": "peripheral-neuropathy",
  "term": "peripheral neuropathy",
  "definition": "Peripheral neuropathy is a disorder of the nerves outside the brain and spinal cord that can cause pain, tingling, numbness, and muscle weakness. It can develop after physical injury or from causes such as toxic substances, viral illness, diabetes, kidney failure, cancer, or certain drugs.",
